/-!
Part `k` of window `i` of function `j` is `[s, J, x, m, c, d, jp, b, u, mo]`: it starts at the
window's statement `s` and code offset `J` (the window's start for the first part), with the
counts of each opcode (in `Opcode`'s order) the walk's paths pass at most up to there, and the
bit set `u` of the callee frame pointer and dispatch target cells they set up, and, for a part
starting inside the segment at `J`, the number `mo` of its items before (`0` if absent). A window
of one part with nothing handed on is `[]`. Checked by `B2C.cplWin`.
